          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: c'era una volta",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "c'era una volta — \"once upon a time (there was)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "C'era una volta una ragazza che viveva nel bosco. Once upon a time there was a girl who lived in the woods."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The opening of almost every fairy tale; c'era is the imperfetto of c'è."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "volta \"a time, a turn\" is built on voltare, usually traced to Vulgar Latin volvitāre, from Latin volvere \"to roll, to turn\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
